sentences.text:
3. The revisionists raised the following grounds:
a) That Ld. Trial Court passed the impugned order mechanically without sifting or weighing or considering the relevancy of the facts, circumstances and submissions and did not consider the material placed on record;
b) That there is not a single incident/allegation by the complainant against the petitioner Pradeep Kumar or his family for her harassment;
c) That there is no demand of dowry, ill-treatment or harassment at the hands of any of the revisionists;
d) That Ld. Trial Court failed to appreciate material contradictions in the statement of complainant;
e) That Ld. Trial Court ignored that revisionist Varun Kumar Singh and his wife Kamlesh were staying separate from complainant and revisionist Pradeep Kumar even before their marriage and there was no reason for them to allegedly harass the complainant for dowry;
f) That there is no legally admissible evidence on record, which prima facie suggest the essential ingredients of offences u/s 406/498-A/34 IPC;

